<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  #163 — the static contrast gate.

  Location: AGP reads the MODULE-level `app/lint.xml` automatically (a file at the
  repository root would be read by no module). Proven: the first `updateLintBaseline`
  run reported its `UnknownIssueId` finding at `app/lint.xml:15`, so this file is
  definitely the one being applied.

  TextContrast (text/background pairs below the WCAG floor) is declared as an ERROR,
  and it is deliberately absent from `lint-baseline.xml`: a baseline entry would
  silence exactly the class of defect this gate exists for. `XmlColorPolicyTest`
  asserts that invariant, so the baseline cannot grow a TextContrast entry unnoticed.

  KNOWN GAP — read this before trusting the line above: lint 32.1.1 (AGP 9.1.1)
  ships NO contrast detector (`lint-checks-32.1.1.jar` contains no `*Contrast*`
  class; `TextContrast` is reported as an unknown issue id). The declaration is
  therefore inert today and only takes effect once the toolchain carries the check
  again. The effective contrast gate in this repository is `XmlColorPolicyTest`
  (palette parity + `recording_*` pairs, both modes) together with the #161/#162
  audits. The `UnknownIssueId` ignore below exists solely so that this forward-
  looking declaration does not turn into a permanent lint config warning.
-->
<lint>
    <issue id="TextContrast" severity="error" />

    <issue id="UnknownIssueId">
        <ignore path="lint.xml" />
    </issue>
</lint>
